Z||000000||brownrt||01-21-2000||10:25 AM||||My 84 2.5, 78,000miles, died on the road, no unusual noise.  My dealer found a screw from the throttle body inside the engine.  Is this a known problem for 84's or is he ripping me off?  How much should I pay for a rebuilt GM engine?||||reg||5
Z||000001||dogtired||01-21-2000||11:22 AM||||Welcome to the Fourm!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Usually a new members first question is "how do I set the clock" or something simple, This is really a tough one  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>I would proceed with CAUTION here, Only one time have I found a bold in the oil pan and the previous owner, told me they had dropped it in (the carb) by accident, it had gone through the manifold and pounded a hole in a piston (an old in line 6 chev).  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I am trying to think of which screw might have done that? And am also thinking the dealer might be trying to do the same to you?<BR>What type of damage is the dealer talking about??? Was the motor locked up?? To have a dealer put in a short block Ill bet you are talking 1,200 to 1,800 bucks?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><BR>Good Luck, and keep us posted!<BR>AGAIN WELCOME!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000002||brownrt||01-21-2000||11:48 AM||||The screw looks like a 6-32x1 inch cap screw.  It is one of 4 that sits on top of the valve body inside the air filter.  I saw the actually screw and where it came from.  It just sounds fishy on how it came out.  My original problem that got the car to the dealer by tow truck, sounds more like one of the other threads about the engine mysteriously shutting off and acting like it has a dead battery.  I also saw the damage.  It damaged the No. 3 piston, scored the intake valve on the same cylinder and damaged the No. 4 piston (the screw broke in to 2 parts).  The dealer wants $3400 for a rebuilt GM engine with 50,000 mile warranty.  I told him I can by an entire Fiero for less.||||reg||1
Z||000003||william_thorniii||01-21-2000||12:39 PM||||You could probably have Ed Parks install a 3.4L for less as well.<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
Z||000004||DRH||01-21-2000||01:19 PM||||Welcome.<P>Since you saw the evidence, it doesn't sound like he's ripping you off about what happened. No way I would pay $3400 for a 2.5 though unless the car has some extreme sentimental value. Even then I believe you can get a better deal. Either a cheaper replacement 2.5 or a LOT better engine as others suggested.<P>Too bad your in DE... I have a totalled 84 with a good engine here in WI...<P>||||reg||1
